"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1K8BE4BSR1S06DWN\",\"title\":\"Project Earthstone — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"UNDER VALIDATION\",\"EW\",\"Project Earthstone\",\"Anglo American\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Expected first certificates\",\"2026\",\"Project code\",\"RV8Q\",\"Crediting period\",\"31 Mar 2026 to 31 Mar 2031\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"RV8Q\",\"approval\":\"\",\"protocol_current\":\"Enhanced Weathering in Agriculture v1.1\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 2 of 2\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"24 May 2026\",\"Public Comment Period Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"23 Apr 2026\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://angloamerican.com\",\"t\":\"Anglo American\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/enhanced-weathering-agriculture/1.1\",\"t\":\"Enhanced Weathering in Agriculture v1.1\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1JQ6W87EZ1S0VHZ8\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/standard#validation-and-verification-process\",\"t\":\"Isometric Standard\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JQ6W87EZ1S0VHZ8/prj_1K8BE4BSR1S06DWN/pjd_1KT91EV2C1S0YCBB/public_comment_period_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JQ6W87EZ1S0VHZ8/prj_1K8BE4BSR1S06DWN/pjd_1KPY04VFC1S004CE/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"UNDER VALIDATION\\nEW\\nProject Earthstone\\nAnglo American\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nExpected first certificates\\n2026\\nProject code\\nRV8Q\\nCrediting period\\n31 Mar 2026 to 31 Mar 2031\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nEnhanced Weathering in Agriculture v1.1\\nSummary\\n\\nThis project is a partnership between mining conglomerate Anglo American plc and ERW developer ZeroEx GmbH which uses material that would otherwise become waste to generate permanent, scalable CDR. Anglo American's Barro Alto facility in Goiás, Brazil, generates roughly 2 million tonnes per year of magnesium silicate, a waste of the nickel production process with very high weathering potential and proven agricultural co-benefits. Project Earthstone collaborates with farmers in the region to apply this material on thousands of hectares of agricultural land, taking advantage of Anglo American's value chain and ZeroEx's measurement expertise.\\n\\nRio Verde, state of Goiás, Brazil\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nEnhanced Weathering (EW) accelerates the Earth's natural chemical weathering process to remove carbon dioxide from the atmosphere. In chemical weathering, carbon dioxide dissolved in rainwater reacts with minerals in rocks, partly dissolving them and producing stable bicarbonate ions. These bicarbonate ions are transported by rivers to the ocean, where they are safely stored for thousands of years. EW is typically carried out by spreading crushed reactive rocks or minerals on croplands.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 22 May 2026\\nPublic comment period\\nCompleted 2026\\nInitial documentation submission\\nCompleted 2026\\nAudit kick-off\\nCompleted 2026\\nSite visit\\nExpected 2026\\nIN PROGRESS\\nApproval date\\n\\nIsometric officially approves the project having reviewed the validation report produced by the VVB, documenting the activities, results, and conclusion of the audit. A full list of content requirements for the report can be found in the Isometric Standard.\\n\\nExpected 2026\\nInitial credit issuance\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n24 May 2026\\tPublic Comment Period Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n23 Apr 2026\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 2 of 2\\nPrevious\\nNext\"}"